.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
gateway/.secrets*

# The seed corpus IS the asset — 28 files, 140K of hand-curated JSON with
# provenance. It is tracked. The original `data/**` rule was written for "large
# blobs" that do not exist in this repository, and would have excluded the most
# expensive, hardest-to-rebuild thing the project owns.
#
# Ignore genuinely large or derived artefacts by name as they appear, not the
# whole tree.
data/**/*.zip
data/**/*.tar.gz
data/**/*.sqlite
data/**/*.dump

# ui/data.js is derived and 673K, but it IS tracked deliberately: --verify is a
# criterion at G1 and G3, and having the bundle in history lets you diff what it
# looked like at each gate. A result is comparable only within the thing that
# produced it.

# "Most recent invocation" files. Calibrate from eval/runs/, eval/answer_runs/
# and eval/sweeps/ — which ARE tracked — never from these.
eval/*_last_run.json

# Upstream gazetteer dumps: re-fetchable, and one is 129 MB. The gazetteer
# built from them (data/gazetteer.json) is the asset and is tracked.
data/pleiades-*.gz
_to_delete/

# Commit-message files for `git commit -F`. Scratch by construction: each one is
# consumed by the commit it describes and its reasoning belongs in the session's
# result document, not in the repository root. Ignored so `git status --short`
# reads clean before a corpus change, where "expect: clean" has to mean it.
commit-*.txt

# FINDING 107. The Claude desktop app writes every file delivered to the chat
# into a "Claude outputs/" folder inside whichever project folder the session is
# connected to -- which here is the repository root. It is NOT a leftover from
# an earlier session: it reappears the moment a file is delivered, so moving it
# out is a chore that never finishes and `git status --short` stops reading
# clean before a corpus change, where "expect: clean" has to mean it.
#
# Ignored rather than fought. Anything worth keeping in it is a screenshot or a
# document that belongs beside the project, not inside the repository, and the
# ones this project has accumulated are in ../Claude outputs/.
Claude outputs/
